/target/
# The oracle virtual environment (testdata/oracles/README.md): development tooling,
# deliberately not a workspace dependency and not checked in. The fixtures it
# generates are.
/.venv-oracles/
/target-alt/
**/target/
/gungnir-journal/
*.jsonl
!docs/**/*.jsonl
!testdata/tracks/samples/**/*.jsonl
# The constructed SAPIENT session (testdata/sapient/SOURCE.md). Three tests in
# gungnir-ingest/tests/sapient_spotter.rs read it, so it is fixture, not journal output.
!testdata/sapient/*.jsonl
/testdata/tracks/full/
/deploy/**/*.local.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Key material. Nothing in this repository may hold a secret or a path to one
# (`docs/release-governance.md`, Hosting). These patterns are a backstop, not the
# policy: a private key should not be inside the working tree in the first place.
/github
/github.pub
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*_rsa
*_ed25519
!**/testdata/**/*.pem

# --- Documents that may be read but not redistributed
# `docs/design/external-standards.md` keeps this distinction per source. STANAG 4609
# is published by the NATO Standardization Office; a reference copy is a working file
# on the drafting host, not repository content.
/4609EFed05.pdf
*.pdf
!docs/**/*.pdf

# --- Editor and tool leavings
.~lock.*#
*.tmp
*.bak
/scratch/

# --- Commercial material, kept out of the repository
# The business plan, financial model, pricing, market and competitive analysis
# (plan 01). Excluded by the owner on 2026-09-07. Documents elsewhere in `docs/`
# still cite this folder; those citations resolve on the drafting host and not in a
# clone, which is a deliberate consequence of the exclusion rather than an oversight.
# A directory excluded outright cannot have anything re-included from it -- git does
# not descend into it -- so the contents are ignored and the one published file is
# named back in.
/docs/business/*
!/docs/business/README.md
